# interplay_session_iosurface: A compositor over the IOSurface host device (map and isolate only: QEMU creates that device only with a memory map, apple-gfx-mmio.c). Two 16 x 8 BGRA surfaces are mapped; task 1 renders frames into them through mapper textures, on the root FIFO and on child 1, and the driver presents each with DisplaySwapMapping (8), double-buffered; the host encodes every frame. The surface's test command writes its pattern between frames. Suspend and resume in the middle: the restore presents the last mapped surface again (GuestDisplay::finish_restore, a new_frame), and the resumed device renders the same frame into the same surface. Teardown deletes the mapper textures before unmapping their surfaces.
